I'm new to this newsgroup, so these may be old complaints..

Having genocided a few monster types, I was a bit miffed when
one of them put an end to an excellent game 30 levels further
down last night.  (Unix nethack V2.3e, on level 50)
Is this a bug? If so, can we expect to see it fixed someday?

Who in their right mind would continue to eat [e.g.] a dragon while
they are being killed? I suggest the remaining food values be assigned
to a "carcass" which can rot like any dead meat, and beg to be allowed
to defend myself in version 3.



Enhancements:
It would be nice if magic traps could *occasionally* have a beneficial
effect, e.g. recharging wands/making spells more legible/restoring
memory after reading scrolls of amnesia .. 
Perhaps this could only happen while the player is confused.

Electric eels might also be able to recharge wands, perhaps if the wand
was *wielded* against the eel..
..and too many attempts might make it too hot to handle for a while..

How about a scroll of "War an Peace" which demands 100 moves to finish
reading the chapter unless attacked... 
(Would one be any the wiser for it?)

It should be mandatory to drink every 2000 moves or so, a water bottle
would then be useful - it could be filled by a 'dip' in a fountain,
although potions should also qualify.
(Perhaps a trip to the bathroom might be in order too- look how much
you eat and drink in a good game! Don't forget that female players will
take at least twice as long as males if they are carrying a mirror!!)

Applying a mirror in direction "." should tell you whether or not it is
cursed- "You see your handsome/beautiful reflection" = cursed


